<title>USA: Amgen gets broader patent for Neupogen.</title>
<headline>Amgen gets broader patent for Neupogen.</headline>
<dateline>THOUSAND OAKS, Calif. 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amgen Inc said Wednesday it has received broader protection for Neupogen from the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office.</p>
<p>The patent, issued on December 3, gives additional protection against unauthorized making, importation, use or sale of recombinant G-CSF, marketed as Neupogen, in the U.S.</p>
<p>The patent provides 17 years of protection.</p>
<p>Neupogen is widely used by cancer chemotheraphy patients.</p>
</text>
